# %% [markdown]
# # Simple MS Simulator — Phase 1: condition grid, merge rule, load projection (Colab)
#
# `specs_simple_ms_simulator/roadmap.md` Phase 1, plan `specs_simple_ms_simulator/phase1_plan.md`.
# **Generated by `build/mk_simple_sim_grid.py` — do not hand-edit.** Runtime: Colab **GPU (A100 or
# L4) + High-RAM**, about 45 min: ~10 min ms-pred install, ~20k + ~20k ICEBERG predictions, the rest I/O.
#
# | step | question | rule (fixed before the numbers are seen) |
# |---|---|---|
# | 1 | which (adduct, CE) conditions does the test pipeline produce? | base CEs = the 20/40/60 ladder if `enveda-np-examples` confirms it, else the single CEs covering ≥ 95 % + every merged constituent |
# | 2 | nearest-grid tolerance | largest Δ ∈ {2.5, 5, 10, 15} eV with median sim(pred@c, pred@c±Δ) ≥ 0.90 |
# | 3 | merged multi-CE spectra | sum-merge vs max-over-CEs, truth ranked in its ±8.5 ppm window; higher MRR wins, ties (≤ 0.01) → max |
# | 4 | pool trimming + on-the-fly load | phase1's stage A/B window on np-examples molecules, bootstrapped to 400 molecules, p95 |
# | 5 | T4 throughput | **Kaggle** notebook `casmi_simple_sim_t4_kaggle.ipynb` → `t4.json`, copied to `_simlib/grid/` |
# | 6 | precompute scope | cheapest of A (none) / B (`[M+H]+`,`[M-H]-`) / C (all covered) whose projected Kaggle time ≤ 6.3 h; none → **STOP** |
#
# Steps 1–4 do not need `t4.json`. Step 6 prints `PENDING` until `t4.json` is on Drive; then re-run
# only the last three code cells (step 5, step 6, report). Outputs: `_simlib/grid/cond_grid.json` and `_simlib/grid/grid_report.json`.
# Paste the final printout back into the chat.

# %%
